    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bb944b51_662872e8",
        "filename": "common/btle_ll.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 651,
      "author": {
        "id": 1156614
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-08-17T20:15:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It does call this function, even if rx_rv !\u003d EC_SUCCESS.  I have it set up so that when an RX occurs in the connection state, this function is always called. If there is a failure in the receive, this will still \"update\" the packet by not changing it--to re-send it. Calling this function also keeps track of metrics and debug information (\"++num_consecutive_nacks_received\").",
      "parentUuid": "bb944b51_3bea0302",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 651,
        "startChar": 53,
        "endLine": 651,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "4c26b24e91797e07c97e85ec8b12c91bc04aa31f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bb944b51_f3cfbf26",
        "filename": "common/btle_ll.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
