      "writtenOn": "2016-08-17T23:47:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This might just be how I think, but it makes more sense to me this way. Every time the ble_rx function is called, it calls this function. This function decides what the data in the packet is supposed to be. It could be a re-sent packet, or it could be new data. It feels less intuitive to me to have this function selectively called. Does that make sense?",
      "parentUuid": "bb944b51_f3cfbf26",
      "range": {
